<figure class="inchy-process-field inchy-process-field--opening">
  <img src="{{ 'inchy-growers-harvest.jpg' | asset_url }}" width="1280" height="854" loading="eager" alt="A Colombian grower holding harvested sacha inchi seed pods">
  <figcaption>THE SEED, THE SOURCE, THE START OF FORM1</figcaption>
</figure>
<section class="inchy-process-step">
  <span class="inchy-process-step__number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
  <header><p class="inchy-process-step__label">SOURCE</p><h2>QUALITY IS DECIDED BEFORE PROCESSING.</h2></header>
  <div class="inchy-process-step__copy">
    <p>Before there is a powder, there is a plant—and someone who tends it. INCHY begins with sacha inchi grown by small farmers in Colombia.</p>
    <p>Consistent, high-quality seed was difficult to source. That is why we helped establish a growers association. Working directly with its members gives us a shared starting point: care for the crop and a commitment to quality.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inchy-process-step">
  <span class="inchy-process-step__number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
  <header><p class="inchy-process-step__label">PRESS</p><h2>THE TRANSFORMATION BEGINS WITH PURPOSE.</h2></header>
  <div class="inchy-process-step__copy">
    <p>Pressing removes part of the seed’s oil and concentrates what remains. But pressing alone does not create FORM1. It creates the material from which our work begins.</p>
    <p>From this point, every decision affects the finished ingredient: its composition, its flavour, its texture and how it behaves in food or drinks.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inchy-process-step">
  <span class="inchy-process-step__number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
  <header><p class="inchy-process-step__label">REFINE</p><h2>TASTE. TEXTURE. POSSIBILITY.</h2></header>
  <div class="inchy-process-step__copy">
    <p>Our proprietary process has been developed over years of working with sacha inchi. Through controlled grinding, drying and finishing, we shape the pressed seed into a consistent functional ingredient.</p>
    <div class="inchy-process-details">
      <div><h3>FLAVOUR</h3><p>Unflavoured means no added flavouring—not no character. We work with the seed’s own flavour rather than disguising it.</p></div>
      <div><h3>TEXTURE</h3><p>Particle size changes what you feel in yoghurt, oats or a blended drink. Texture is engineered alongside composition.</p></div>
      <div><h3>USE</h3><p>FORM1 is developed to enter food and drinks you already enjoy. A useful ingredient must work beyond a nutrition panel.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inchy-process-step">
  <span class="inchy-process-step__number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
  <header><p class="inchy-process-step__label">PRESERVE</p><h2>PROTEIN + FIBER. ONE FOOD ORIGIN.</h2></header>
  <div class="inchy-process-step__copy">
    <p>Protein and fiber begin together in the seed. We keep both in the finished ingredient. FORM1 is not a protein isolate with fiber added back later; both come from the same sacha inchi starting material.</p>
    <p>Processing changes the seed’s structure. Our purpose is not to pretend otherwise. It is to carry this protein–fiber relationship into a more useful form.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inchy-process-step inchy-process-step--result">
  <span class="inchy-process-step__number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
  <header><p class="inchy-process-step__label">FORM1</p><h2>NOT SIMPLY SACHA INCHI FLOUR.</h2></header>
  <div class="inchy-process-step__copy">
    <p>Sacha inchi flours and proteins can share a name while differing greatly in sourcing, processing, flavour, texture and function. The raw material matters. What happens to it matters just as much.</p>
    <p>FORM1 is the result of controlling that journey: direct sourcing, a proprietary multi-stage process, protein and fiber retained from one seed, and development centred on everyday use.</p>
    <p class="inchy-process-conclusion">THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT SACHA INCHI ALONE.<br>IT IS WHAT WE ASK OF EVERY STEP.</p>
    <a class="inchy-text-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=how-to-use">FIND YOUR ROUTINE →</a>
  </div>
</section>
